cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Is Honesty the Best Policy in Negotiation? The Influence of Lying in Colored Trails (simulation code)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SverreBr/MasterThesis"
abstract: >-
  Java code of agent-based simulations of negotiation in the Colored Trails game,
  in which agents with zeroth-, first-, or second-order theory of mind can send
  goal location messages, and in which agents can be honest, misleading, or lying.
  The repository contains a GUI to inspect single negotiations, the code of the
  simulation experiments of the master's thesis "The influence of lying in a
  negotiation setting: Colored Trails" (Brok, 2023, University of Groningen), and
  Jupyter notebooks for part of the analysis. The article "Is Honesty the Best
  Policy in Negotiation? The Influence of Lying in Colored Trails" (Brok,
  Verbrugge, and de Weerd, Autonomous Agents and Multi-Agent Systems) reports
  simulation results of the thesis.
